Okay... how about scrapping the wands and letting shopkeepers cast
attack spells?  That way, you can give them any magical ranged attack
you want without having to worry about players killing shopkeepers
just to get those attacks for themselves.  Maybe leave them a wand or
two for backup, just in case they get cancelled...

(This reminds me of a discussion at a con recently, about where all
those high-level NPC tavernkeepers in many RPG settings come from --
the obvious answer being that they're former high-level adventurers
who settled down and got themselves a wife, some kids and a decent
job.  If that's true of nethack's shopkeepers as well, they damn well
_ought_ to be able to kick some serious player ass.)

